@template brisk
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks (see banks/clock.lines for the keys).

== work.clock.in
- Morning. Board's up. Take the top one.
- Eight sharp. Good. Scrubbers first.
- On time. Keep it that way.

== work.clock.out
- Done. Good shift. Go eat.
- Clocked out. Rest. Back at eight.
- Board's shorter than this morning. That's the job.

== work.clock.monday
- Monday. Good weekend? Short answer. Jobs waiting.
- Rested? Good. Week starts now.

== work.clock.friday
- Week done. Rest properly. Monday, eight.
- Weekend. Plans? Make some. Then rest.

== work.clock.back
- Back. Good. Easy job first. Then normal.   #warm
- Welcome back. We managed. Barely.   #funny
